# Assertions about individuals — every spelling DLe accepts.
#
# This document exists to be read, and it deliberately uses several spellings of the same
# axiom shape, so it does not round-trip byte for byte. The writer picks one form per kind:
# `rex:Cat`, `ex:ada:Person` and `bob : Person` are all class assertions, and all three come
# back spaced. What must survive is the set of axioms, which is what the CI regression job
# compares.
#
# The forms follow Introduction to Description Logic:
#
#   a : C          a is a C, where C may be any concept expression
#   (a,b):r        a is related to b by the object property r
#   ¬(a,b):r       a is not related to b by r
#   (a,v):d        a's data property d has the value v
#   ¬(a,v):d       a's d does not have the value v
#   a = b          a and b are the same individual
#   a ≠ b          a and b are different individuals
#
# A class assertion may also be written without the space — `rex:Cat` — which is the
# textbook spelling. It is read as an assertion only when the part before the colon is not
# a declared prefix, because otherwise those characters are a prefixed name. Written output
# always spaces it, so the meaning never depends on the prefix declarations.
#
# A digit-initial name in the default namespace carries its own colon, so a statement about
# one has two: `(bob,rex)::762705008`. A digit-initial class needs the space as well.
#
# There are no comments below this header on purpose. A comment attaches to the entity
# named by the statement under it, and several statements here share a subject, so section
# headings would merge into one another — see the notes on comment fidelity in the issue
# tracker rather than reading anything into their absence.

@ontology <http://example.org/abox-forms>
@prefix : <http://example.org/abox#>
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/other#>

Cat ⊑ Animal
Dog ⊑ Animal
Animal ⊑ ⊤
Keeper ⊑ Person
∃hasPet.⊤ ⊑ Person
⊤ ⊑ ∀hasPet.Animal
∃age.⊤ ⊑ Animal
⊤ ⊑ ∀age.xsd:integer
⊤ ⊑ ∀nickname.xsd:string
Func(age)
∃caresFor.⊤ ⊑ Keeper
⊤ ⊑ ∀caresFor.Animal
hasPet ⊑ caresFor

bob : Person
rex:Cat
ex:ada:Person
ex:zoe:ex:Keeper
mia : :762705008
bob : Person ⊓ ¬Keeper
rex : Cat ⊔ Dog
bob : ∃hasPet.Cat
bob : ≥1 hasPet.Animal
ada : ∀hasPet.Animal
zoe : ¬Cat

(bob,rex):hasPet
(ex:ada,rex):hasPet
(ex:zoe,rex):caresFor
¬(ex:zoe,rex):hasPet
(bob,rex)::762705008
¬(mia,rex)::762705008

(rex,7):age
(rex,"Rexie"):nickname
(rex,"Rexie le chien"@fr):nickname
(rex,""):nickname
(rex,"says \"woof\""):nickname
¬(bob,"Bobby"):nickname
¬(rex,3):age

bob = robert
mia ≠ zoe
rex = rexie = rexthedog
bob ≠ mia ≠ zoe

@label bob "Bob"
@label ex:ada "Ada"@en
@doc rex "A dog, asserted several ways to exercise the reader."
@ann mia rdfs:seeAlso "https://example.org/mia"
